# Deploy — one build, one rollout

# The shapes a `>` line takes: the element itself, as the first child of a step
# and as the block that opens the document. It also pins the fallback — a `>`
# with nothing under it is a line, not an accordion — so both implementations
# keep counting it the same way.

> shell transcript
  $ bundle exec rake db:migrate
  the only irreversible step

gate: ready
  yes:
    > Charge.create(amount:, source:)   @lib/charge.rb:9
      # the only irreversible step
      - 900ms p99, 30s timeout
      > retries reuse the idempotency key
    > bare accordion, nothing under it
    - Sidekiq.push(job)
      > a nested accordion
        - detail line
